class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: platform/posix parses lines of /etc/passwd's and /etc/group's form given on standard input, refusing a comment, an NIS line, a field missing or too many, an empty name and an ID that is not a decimal below 0xFFFFFFFF, and skipping empty member names; then looks root and group zero up by ID and by name in the real databases, through /etc/passwd and /etc/group on a static Linux program and the C library elsewhere, finds the process's own account by name when it has one, and refuses an ID and a name no database holds, a name holding a colon and a buffer too small with ERANGE
program: main.ldn
root: ../../../../..
stdin: database.txt
run_expect: output.txt
stream: output
status: 42
constructs: 0940, 1030, 1660
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, macos-arm64, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, linux-rv64
